    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42) serving as our undisputed pillars of production. Both benefit from a high-ceiling matchup against Springs; **Trea Turner** is a must-start due to his elite sprint speed and the advantage provided by the pitcher's slow delivery, which maximizes his SB potential in a category where we cannot afford to fall behind. **Kyle Schwarber** remains a powerhouse play, with his 0.394 xwOBA aligning perfectly with favorable wind conditions. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.70) offers significant value as a high-upside play against Singer; his aggressive base-running dynamic and a strong platoon edge solidify his position despite hitting lower in the order.\n\nWhile our starting nine remains aggressive, the tightest decision centered on the utility slot. **Junior Caminero** (62.36) edged out the bench group, though the optimizer closely scrutinized the limited opportunities for **Luke Raley**, who ultimately sits due to a lack of a clear platoon advantage today. We remain cautious regarding **Dillon Dingler** (40.78), whose score is suppressed by a negative platoon split against Gray, putting him near our usage floor; we are monitoring his performance closely to ensure he doesn't jeopardize our game cap efficiency. The rest of the lineup\u2014including **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Carson Benge**, **Yordan Alvarez**, and **Hyeseong Kim**\u2014all project as solid contributors. We are keeping **Christian Yelich** on the IL and **Zac Veen** in the minors, while **Gary Sanchez** remains benched alongside **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** as we await more favorable platoon environments for their profiles.",
